  "city_retention": {
    "threshold_completeness": 0.8,
    "threshold_min_labelled_days": 730,
    "threshold_justification": "Two independent gates are applied. The completeness gate (80% of the calendar days in a city's own observation span must carry a labelled AQI) ensures that per-city lag and rolling features are computed over a near-contiguous series rather than across long gaps, since a lag of one row is only a lag of one day when the series is dense. The volume gate (at least 730 labelled days, i.e. two years) ensures each retained city contributes at least two full annual cycles, so that seasonal structure is estimable and a time-ordered split leaves a usable test period. Both thresholds were fixed before any model was fitted and are not tuned against model performance.",
